WASHINGTON, DC – Congresswoman Eleanor Holmes Norton (D-DC) will hold a “Save D.C. Home Rule” press conference today with national groups whose issues have been attacked in the past using the District of Columbia as a vehicle.  The national organizations – American Civil Liberties Union, NARAL Pro-Choice America, Planned Parenthood Federation of America, Brady Campaign to Prevent Gun Violence, and AIDS United – will discuss their intentions to use their nationwide networks, along with another 100 pro-D.C. home rule organizations, to contact members of the House and Senate appropriations committees to protect D.C.’s right to spend its local funds without congressional interference in the upcoming fiscal year 2015 D.C. appropriations bill. 
